  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions will continue through mid-week before we see \na pattern change with the chance for some rain. The first half of \nthe week will be relatively drier which will help keep heat index \nvalues in check. As we get into mid-week however, moisture will \nbegin to increase which could bump those heat index values above \nheat advisory criteria. Although conditions will be drier the first \nhalf of the week, some areas could briefly see heat index values \nclimb to over 109 degrees. Remember that cumulative heat stress can \nresult in a higher risk of heat illness. Please use caution if you \nare spending time outside. Drink plenty of water and take breaks. \nDon't forget to look before you lock! The pattern change is expected \nlate this week as the increased moisture interacts with an \napproaching mid-level trough yielding low chances for rain. \n\n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat&&",
